---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DetailCard from '../components/DetailCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Courses"
  description="Coursework at Purdue — probability, statistics, analysis, and the math underneath risk modeling."
>
  <h1>Courses</h1>
  <p>
    Selected coursework from my DS &amp; Math double major at Purdue. The throughline: I want the
    theory underneath risk models, not just the tooling — probability, statistics, and the
    numerics that make a model trustworthy.
  </p>

  <DetailCard
    title="Probability"
    meta="Purdue · completed"
    summary="Random variables, distributions, expectation, limit theorems."
  >
    <p>
      The foundation everything else on this page builds on — distributions, conditioning,
      expectation, and the limit theorems that make statistics work.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>

  <DetailCard
    title="Statistics in R"
    meta="Purdue · completed"
    summary="Applied statistical computing and inference in R."
  >
    <p>
      Hands-on statistical inference in R — estimation, hypothesis testing, and regression on
      real datasets.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>

  <DetailCard
    title="Data Science"
    meta="Purdue · completed"
    summary="The end-to-end workflow: wrangling, modeling, validation."
  >
    <p>
      The complete pipeline from raw data to defensible conclusions — data wrangling, modeling,
      and validation.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>

  <DetailCard
    title="Real Analysis"
    meta="Purdue · completed"
    summary="Rigor: limits, continuity, convergence, proof-writing."
  >
    <p>
      Proof-based analysis — the course that teaches you what the calculus you learned actually
      says, and how to argue it precisely.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>

  <DetailCard
    title="Linear Algebra"
    meta="Purdue · completed"
    summary="Vector spaces, eigenvalues, decompositions."
  >
    <p>
      Vector spaces, linear maps, and eigendecompositions — the language most of machine learning
      is written in.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>

  <DetailCard
    title="Stochastic Calculus"
    meta="Self-study"
    summary="Brownian motion, Itô calculus, SDEs — taught myself."
  >
    <p>
      Self-taught: Brownian motion, Itô integration, and stochastic differential equations — the
      mathematics underneath volatility, derivatives pricing, and modern risk models.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>

  <h2>Up next (2026–27)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Statistical Theory</li>
    <li>Numerical Methods</li>
    <li>Advanced Linear Algebra</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
